IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ba-house`

-- Building Act 2011 (WA) -- the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as parameters (the Q&A layer).
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. The baseline (ba-house.l4) was written from the seat of the home owner having a house built (an "owner" of the
-- land, s 5). That is the first role; an owner who is also the named builder (an owner-builder) stays in it, with the
-- baseline's `is named as the builder on the building permit`. The second is the builder named on the building permit,
-- the "responsible person" (s 31): s 9 binds "a person" who does building work, s 16(c) makes the builder sign the
-- application, s 28(1)(a) gives them the permit, and ss 33, 34 and 37(1) put the notices of completion and cessation and
-- the building standards on them. The third is the occupier, a tenant or licensee (s 40), whom s 41 forbids to occupy or
-- use a building without an occupancy permit. The permit authority, the building surveyor, the Building Commissioner and
-- the State Administrative Tribunal are never a seat: what they may or must do appears as what it means for the person.
--
-- SITUATIONS (graffiti design D8). Within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that situation's fact
-- straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when it does not hold, without reading anything else.
-- The questions of one situation share ONE input, the same name, type and @desc, so the form asks it once:
--   - `my building permit application was refused` (owner): the s 24 notice of the refusal and its reasons.
--   - `the named builder has given notice of ceasing to act on the permit` (owner, builder): the owner's copy of the
--     notice of cessation, and the builder's duty to give it and its fine (s 34(3)).
-- A question that arises in every situation of its role takes no situation input. The baseline's own inputs that look
-- like situations (`a decision has been made` for s 23, the Work, Building and Person records) are kept as they are, so
-- that the answers are the baseline's.
--
-- The rules are the baseline's. This module calls the baseline's functions and restates none. The builder's and the
-- occupier's answers come from the same functions, given the baseline's Person record for that seat (a fixed value: the
-- named builder who is not an owner; an occupier who is not an owner). The two builder questions of s 34(3) are helpers
-- here. Every answer type carries `does not arise for you`. No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Building Act 2011 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I own the land the building is on, or will be on`
    `I am the builder named on the building permit`
    `I live in or use the building as a tenant or licensee`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Months` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    months HAS `number of months` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Days` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    days HAS `number of days` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Years` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    years HAS `number of years` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Certificate source answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the certificate comes from` HAS `the source` IS A `Where the certificate of design compliance comes from`

DECLARE `Certificate answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the certificate needed is` HAS `the certificate` IS A `Compliance certificate`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- The baseline's Person record for the two new seats. Neither is an owner of the land (an owner chooses the first role).
`the named builder, not an owner` MEANS Person WITH
    `is registered as a proprietor of the land` IS FALSE
    `holds a prescribed interest in the land` IS FALSE
    `is named as the builder on the building permit` IS TRUE

`an occupier, not an owner` MEANS Person WITH
    `is registered as a proprietor of the land` IS FALSE
    `holds a prescribed interest in the land` IS FALSE
    `is named as the builder on the building permit` IS FALSE

§§ `For the owner, and for the builder`

§§§ `ss 3, 4, 9, 11, 12 -- building work, the building permit, and building without one`

@export Is what I plan to do "building work" (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 3)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the work` IS A Work @desc The work: what kind it is, whether the regulations or a Ministerial order say it needs no building permit, whether it is to stand no longer than a month and whether the public will use it, whether it is done under a building order, and whether a building permit is in effect for it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is what I plan to do building work` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `yes if` (`Is it building work` `the work`)
    WHEN `I am the builder named on the building permit` THEN `yes if` (`Is it building work` `the work`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does this work need a building permit (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 9)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the work` IS A Work @desc The work: what kind it is, whether the regulations or a Ministerial order say it needs no building permit, whether it is to stand no longer than a month and whether the public will use it, whether it is done under a building order, and whether a building permit is in effect for it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does this work need a building permit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `yes if` (`Do I need a building permit` `the work`)
    WHEN `I am the builder named on the building permit` THEN `yes if` (`Do I need a building permit` `the work`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 9: "A person must not do building work unless" a permit is in effect or not required: the owner who does it (or has
-- it done) and the builder who does it are both within it.
@export Would doing this work be the offence of building without a permit, allowing for the defences (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 9; ss 11, 12)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the work` IS A Work @desc The work: what kind it is, whether the regulations or a Ministerial order say it needs no building permit, whether it is to stand no longer than a month and whether the public will use it, whether it is done under a building order, and whether a building permit is in effect for it
      `the permit was suspended and I neither knew nor could reasonably have known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the permit was suspended (the builder ceased or lost registration) without your knowing, or any reasonable way of knowing (s 11)
      `it was emergency work and I applied for a permit as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was emergency protection work under ss 78-80 and a permit was applied for as soon as practicable afterwards (s 12)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Would this work be the offence of building without a permit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `yes if` (`Would doing the work be an offence` `the work` `the permit was suspended and I neither knew nor could reasonably have known` `it was emergency work and I applied for a permit as soon as practicable`)
    WHEN `I am the builder named on the building permit` THEN `yes if` (`Would doing the work be an offence` `the work` `the permit was suspended and I neither knew nor could reasonably have known` `it was emergency work and I applied for a permit as soon as practicable`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my building surveyor an independent building surveyor, neither an owner or the builder nor employed by one (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the surveyor` IS A Surveyor @desc The building surveyor who signs the certificate of design compliance: whether they are an owner of the land or an owner's employee, the proposed builder or the builder's employee, and whether the Registration Act entitles them to sign for this kind of building
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the building surveyor independent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `yes if` (`Is my building surveyor independent` `the surveyor`)
    WHEN `I am the builder named on the building permit` THEN `yes if` (`Is my building surveyor independent` `the surveyor`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 16, 28, 32 -- signing the application, the permit, and how long it lasts`

@export Must I sign the application for the building permit (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 16(b), (c))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A Person @desc You: whether you are a registered proprietor of the land, hold a prescribed interest in it, or are to be named as the builder on the permit
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I sign the application for the building permit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `yes if` (`Must I sign the building permit application` `me`)
    WHEN `I am the builder named on the building permit` THEN `yes if` (`Must I sign the building permit application` `the named builder, not an owner`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I be given the building permit document (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 28(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A Person @desc You: whether you are a registered proprietor of the land, hold a prescribed interest in it, or are to be named as the builder on the permit
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I be given the building permit document` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `yes if` (`Must I be given the building permit` `me`)
    WHEN `I am the builder named on the building permit` THEN `yes if` (`Must I be given the building permit` `the named builder, not an owner`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export For how many years does the building permit have effect (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 32)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the period set out in the permit, in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The period stated on the permit, in years (0 if none is stated)
GIVETH A `Years`
`For how many years does the building permit have effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN years (`For how many years does my building permit last` `the period set out in the permit, in years`)
    WHEN `I am the builder named on the building permit` THEN years (`For how many years does my building permit last` `the period set out in the permit, in years`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 33, 34, 37 -- completion, cessation, and the building standards`

@export Within how many days of completion must I give the permit authority notice of completion (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 33(1))? (0 means it is not my duty)
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A Person @desc You: whether you are a registered proprietor of the land, hold a prescribed interest in it, or are to be named as the builder on the permit
GIVETH A `Days`
`Within how many days of completion must I give notice of completion` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN days (`Within how many days must I give the notice of completion` `me`)
    WHEN `I am the builder named on the building permit` THEN days (`Within how many days must I give the notice of completion` `the named builder, not an owner`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most the builder named on the permit can be fined for not giving notice of completion in time (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 33(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for not giving notice of completion in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN amount `What is the most I can be fined for not giving notice of completion`
    WHEN `I am the builder named on the building permit` THEN amount `What is the most I can be fined for not giving notice of completion`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I ensure that the completed building complies with every applicable building standard (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 37)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A Person @desc You: whether you are a registered proprietor of the land, hold a prescribed interest in it, or are to be named as the builder on the permit
      `the work` IS A Work @desc The work: what kind it is, whether the regulations or a Ministerial order say it needs no building permit, whether it is to stand no longer than a month and whether the public will use it, whether it is done under a building order, and whether a building permit is in effect for it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I ensure the completed building meets the building standards` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `yes if` (`Must I ensure the finished house meets the building standards` `me` `the work`)
    WHEN `I am the builder named on the building permit` THEN `yes if` (`Must I ensure the finished house meets the building standards` `the named builder, not an owner` `the work`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- Situation: the named builder has given the permit authority a notice of cessation (s 34(1)).
@export If my builder stops acting on the permit, within how many days must I be given a copy of the notice of cessation (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 34(3))? (0 means none is owed to me)
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the named builder has given notice of ceasing to act on the permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the builder named on the permit (you, if you are that builder) has given the permit authority a notice of cessation, before the work was completed (s 34(1))
      `me` IS A Person @desc You: whether you are a registered proprietor of the land, hold a prescribed interest in it, or are to be named as the builder on the permit
GIVETH A `Days`
`Within how many days must I be given a copy of the notice of cessation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN
        IF `the named builder has given notice of ceasing to act on the permit`
        THEN days (`Within how many days must I get the notice of cessation` `me`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- Helpers (not in the baseline): s 34(3), the builder's side. "A responsible person must, within 7 days of giving a
-- notice of cessation to a relevant permit authority, give a copy of the notice to an owner ... Penalty: a fine of
-- $10 000."
`s 34(3) -- the days to give an owner a copy of the notice of cessation` MEANS 7
`s 34(3) -- the fine for not giving the copy` MEANS 10000

@export Within how many days of giving the permit authority my notice of cessation must I give an owner a copy (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 34(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the named builder has given notice of ceasing to act on the permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the builder named on the permit (you, if you are that builder) has given the permit authority a notice of cessation, before the work was completed (s 34(1))
GIVETH A `Days`
`Within how many days must I give the owner a copy of my notice of cessation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the builder named on the building permit` THEN
        IF `the named builder has given notice of ceasing to act on the permit`
        THEN days `s 34(3) -- the days to give an owner a copy of the notice of cessation`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for not giving an owner a copy of my notice of cessation in time (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 34(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the named builder has given notice of ceasing to act on the permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the builder named on the permit (you, if you are that builder) has given the permit authority a notice of cessation, before the work was completed (s 34(1))
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for not giving the owner a copy of the notice of cessation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the builder named on the building permit` THEN
        IF `the named builder has given notice of ceasing to act on the permit`
        THEN amount `s 34(3) -- the fine for not giving the copy`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For everyone the Act can prosecute`

§§§ `ss 9, 37, 41, 133 -- penalties, and how long a prosecution may be brought`

@export What is the most I can be fined for building without a permit, a building not meeting the standards, or occupying without an occupancy permit, in dollars (Building Act 2011 (WA) ss 9, 37, 41)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `previous offences` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times you have offended against the same section before
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined under ss 9, 37 or 41` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN amount (`What is the most I can be fined` `previous offences`)
    WHEN `I am the builder named on the building permit` THEN amount (`What is the most I can be fined` `previous offences`)
    WHEN `I live in or use the building as a tenant or licensee` THEN amount (`What is the most I can be fined` `previous offences`)

@export For a third or later offence of building without a permit, a building not meeting the standards, or occupying without an occupancy permit, for how many months at most may I also be imprisoned (Building Act 2011 (WA) ss 9, 37, 41)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `previous offences` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times you have offended against the same section before
GIVETH A `Months`
`For how many months at most may I be imprisoned under ss 9, 37 or 41` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN months (`What is the longest I can be imprisoned in months` `previous offences`)
    WHEN `I am the builder named on the building permit` THEN months (`What is the longest I can be imprisoned in months` `previous offences`)
    WHEN `I live in or use the building as a tenant or licensee` THEN months (`What is the longest I can be imprisoned in months` `previous offences`)

@export Can I still be prosecuted for this offence, this many years after it (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 133(3), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence alleged: building without a building permit (s 9), an owner's completed building not meeting the standards (s 37(2)), occupying without an occupancy permit (s 41), or not giving notice of completion (s 33)
      `years since the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years ago the offence was allegedly committed
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I still be prosecuted for this offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `yes if` (`Can I still be prosecuted` `the offence` `years since the offence`)
    WHEN `I am the builder named on the building permit` THEN `yes if` (`Can I still be prosecuted` `the offence` `years since the offence`)
    WHEN `I live in or use the building as a tenant or licensee` THEN `yes if` (`Can I still be prosecuted` `the offence` `years since the offence`)

§§ `For the owner of the land`

§§§ `s 5 -- am I an owner`

@export Am I an "owner" of the land (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 5)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A Person @desc You: whether you are a registered proprietor of the land, hold a prescribed interest in it, or are to be named as the builder on the permit
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I an owner of the land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `yes if` (`Am I an owner` `me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 14, 16, 17, 20 -- applying, the certificate of design compliance, and the grant`

@export May I make an uncertified application for this building (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 14(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `its classification is prescribed for uncertified applications` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations prescribe the building's classification (for example Class 1a, a house) for uncertified applications
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I make an uncertified application for this building` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `yes if` (`May I make an uncertified application` `its classification is prescribed for uncertified applications`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Where does my certificate of design compliance come from (Building Act 2011 (WA) ss 16(e), (h), 17)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the application` IS A `Kind of application` @desc Whether you apply with a certificate already signed (certified) or without (uncertified)
GIVETH A `Certificate source answer`
`Where does the certificate of design compliance come from` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `the certificate comes from` (`Where does my certificate of design compliance come from` `the application`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must the permit authority grant my building permit (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 20)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the permit application` IS A `Building permit application` @desc Your application and what the permit authority is satisfied of: s 16 complied with, the builder registered or an owner-builder, the certificate of design compliance and its surveyor, home indemnity insurance, the building services levy, and the other matters in s 20(1)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the permit authority grant my building permit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `yes if` (`Must my building permit be granted` `the permit application`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 23, 24, 119 -- the decision, a refusal, and review`

@export Is my building permit application taken to have been refused, because no decision was made in time (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 23(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `days since I applied` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since you applied, counting from the day after
      `the prescribed period in days` IS A NUMBER @desc The period the regulations prescribe for this classification
      `a decision has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the permit authority has decided
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my building permit application taken to have been refused` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `yes if` (`Is my application taken to be refused` `days since I applied` `the prescribed period in days` `a decision has been made`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my application fee be refunded because no decision was made in time (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 23(4), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `days since I applied` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since you applied, counting from the day after
      `the prescribed period in days` IS A NUMBER @desc The period the regulations prescribe for this classification
      `a decision has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the permit authority has decided
      `I did not give further information asked for in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authority refused to consider your application because you did not give information it asked for within the time set
      `the Heritage Council's advice is outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application was referred under the Heritage Act 2018 and the advice has not come back in time
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my building permit application fee be refunded` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `yes if` (`Must my fee be refunded` `days since I applied` `the prescribed period in days` `a decision has been made` `I did not give further information asked for in time` `the Heritage Council's advice is outstanding`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- Situation: the permit authority decided to refuse the building permit (s 24 is tied to "a decision to refuse").
@export Within how many days of refusing my building permit must the permit authority give me written notice, its reasons and my right of review (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 24)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my building permit application was refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the permit authority has decided to refuse to grant your building permit
GIVETH A `Days`
`Within how many days must I be told why my building permit was refused` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN
        IF `my building permit application was refused`
        THEN days `Within how many days must I be told why I was refused`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I ask the State Administrative Tribunal to review a refusal of, or a condition on, my building permit (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 119)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I applied for the permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were the applicant
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I ask the Tribunal to review my building permit decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `yes if` (`May I ask the Tribunal to review` `I applied for the permit`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 41, 54, 63 -- the occupancy permit`

@export Must my new house have an occupancy permit before we move in (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 41; s 66(5); s 69)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the building` IS A Building @desc The building: whether it is finished, whether an occupancy permit or a temporary one is in effect, whether the regulations or a Ministerial order say it needs none, and whether it is to stand no longer than a month and is closed to the public
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my new house have an occupancy permit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `yes if` (`Must the house have an occupancy permit` `the building`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Which certificate must accompany my occupancy permit application (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 54(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the occupancy application` IS A `Kind of occupancy permit application` @desc What the occupancy permit is for: a completed building (s 46), an incomplete building (s 47), or a building with unauthorised work (s 51)
GIVETH A `Certificate answer`
`Which certificate must go with my occupancy permit application` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `the certificate needed is` (`Which certificate must accompany my occupancy permit application` `the occupancy application`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I sign the occupancy permit application, and be given the permit (Building Act 2011 (WA) ss 54(1)(b), 63)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A Person @desc You: whether you are a registered proprietor of the land, hold a prescribed interest in it, or are to be named as the builder on the permit
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I sign the occupancy permit application and be given the permit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `yes if` (`Must I sign the occupancy permit application` `me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the owner, and for the occupier`

§§§ `s 41 -- moving in`

@export May we move in, or let someone else live in or use the building (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 41(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the building` IS A Building @desc The building: whether it is finished, whether an occupancy permit or a temporary one is in effect, whether the regulations or a Ministerial order say it needs none, and whether it is to stand no longer than a month and is closed to the public
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May we move in or let the building be used` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `yes if` (`May we move in` `the building`)
    WHEN `I live in or use the building as a tenant or licensee` THEN `yes if` (`May we move in` `the building`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The owner answers whether they also occupy under a lease or licence, as the baseline asks; the occupier is one by
-- their role (s 40), and is given the baseline's occupier, not an owner.
@export Would moving in, or letting someone else live in or use the building, be an offence (Building Act 2011 (WA) s 41)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A Person @desc You: whether you are a registered proprietor of the land, hold a prescribed interest in it, or are to be named as the builder on the permit
      `I occupy it under a lease, tenancy agreement or licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live in or use the building as a tenant or licensee (an occupier, s 40)
      `the building` IS A Building @desc The building: whether it is finished, whether an occupancy permit or a temporary one is in effect, whether the regulations or a Ministerial order say it needs none, and whether it is to stand no longer than a month and is closed to the public
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Would moving in or letting the building be used be an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own the land the building is on, or will be on` THEN `yes if` (`Would moving in be an offence` `me` `I occupy it under a lease, tenancy agreement or licence` `the building`)
    WHEN `I live in or use the building as a tenant or licensee` THEN `yes if` (`Would moving in be an offence` `an occupier, not an owner` TRUE `the building`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
